184 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 126 0 R
/T (Dairy cooperatives and milk-collection centres gather milk twice a day from many small farmers. Each collection has to be measured for quantity, fat percentage and SNF \(solids-not-fat\) percentage, priced according to a rate chart, and eventually paid out to the farmer. In many centres this information still lives in paper registers or unconnected spreadsheets, which leads to lost records, slow payment calculation and no reliable health history for the animals.)
/E (Dairy cooperatives and milk-collection centres gather milk twice a day from many small farmers. Each collection has to be measured for quantity, fat percentage and SNF \(solids-not-fat\) percentage, priced according to a rate chart, and eventually paid out to the farmer. In many centres this information still lives in paper registers or unconnected spreadsheets, which leads to lost records, slow payment calculation and no reliable health history for the animals.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
185 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 126 0 R
/T (This project designs and implements a relational database, dairy_farm_db, for a dairy farm herd and milk collection system. The database has six normalised tables \(Farmer, Cattle, Milk Collection, Rate Chart, Payment and Health Record\) linked by primary and foreign keys. A web interface built with HTML, CSS and JavaScript, served by a Node.js and Express backend, connects to MySQL and lets a user view, insert and delete records in every table. The amount due to each farmer is calculated entirely in SQL by joining collection entries to the rate band that matches the fat percentage.)
/E (This project designs and implements a relational database, dairy_farm_db, for a dairy farm herd and milk collection system. The database has six normalised tables \(Farmer, Cattle, Milk Collection, Rate Chart, Payment and Health Record\) linked by primary and foreign keys. A web interface built with HTML, CSS and JavaScript, served by a Node.js and Express backend, connects to MySQL and lets a user view, insert and delete records in every table. The amount due to each farmer is calculated entirely in SQL by joining collection entries to the rate band that matches the fat percentage.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
