/T (India is the largest milk producer in the world, and most of that milk comes from small and marginal farmers who each keep a handful of animals. Village-level collection centres and dairy cooperatives gather milk every morning and evening, test it, and pay the farmers periodically. The price paid for a litre of milk is not fixed: it depends on the fat and SNF content found in the sample, so every single delivery has to be recorded with its quantity and quality readings.)
/E (India is the largest milk producer in the world, and most of that milk comes from small and marginal farmers who each keep a handful of animals. Village-level collection centres and dairy cooperatives gather milk every morning and evening, test it, and pay the farmers periodically. The price paid for a litre of milk is not fixed: it depends on the fat and SNF content found in the sample, so every single delivery has to be recorded with its quantity and quality readings.)
/Pg 12 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
