334 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 130 0 R
/T (First Normal Form \(1NF\). Every attribute holds a single atomic value and there are no repeating groups. A farmer's several animals are stored as separate rows of CATTLE instead of a comma- separated list, and repeated deliveries are separate rows of MILK_COLLECTION. Every table has a primary key.)
/E (First Normal Form \(1NF\). Every attribute holds a single atomic value and there are no repeating groups. A farmer's several animals are stored as separate rows of CATTLE instead of a comma- separated list, and repeated deliveries are separate rows of MILK_COLLECTION. Every table has a primary key.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [16]
>>
endobj
335 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 130 0 R
/T (Second Normal Form \(2NF\). All tables use a single-column primary key, so partial dependency on part of a composite key cannot occur. Every non-key attribute depends on the whole key.)
/E (Second Normal Form \(2NF\). All tables use a single-column primary key, so partial dependency on part of a composite key cannot occur. Every non-key attribute depends on the whole key.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [17]
>>
endobj
336 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /H3
/P 130 0 R
/T (Third Normal Form \(3NF\). There are no transitive dependencies. Farmer details are stored only in FARMER and referred to by farmer_id elsewhere. Prices are stored only in RATE_CHART and are not copied into each collection row. Animal details live only in CATTLE. In every table, non-key attributes depend only on the key.)
/E (Third Normal Form \(3NF\). There are no transitive dependencies. Farmer details are stored only in FARMER and referred to by farmer_id elsewhere. Prices are stored only in RATE_CHART and are not copied into each collection row. Animal details live only in CATTLE. In every table, non-key attributes depend only on the key.)
/Pg 16 0 R
/K [18]
>>
endobj
