1211 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 150 0 R
/E (ER model was converted into six tables in Third Normal Form, with primary keys, foreign keys, unique and NOT NULL constraints, and referential actions that protect important history. The amount due to every farmer is computed by a single SQL join against the rate chart, replacing manual lookup. The web interface connected to MySQL lets a user view, insert and delete records in every table, and the database itself rejects invalid operations such as deleting a farmer who still has records.)
/Pg 36 0 R
/K [26]
>>
endobj
1212 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 150 0 R
/E (Working on the project showed how design choices affect correctness. Making the rate bands non- overlapping prevents a boundary value from being counted twice, and storing payments as settled snapshots keeps history stable when rates change.)
/Pg 36 0 R
/K [27]
>>
endobj
