2330 0 obj
<<
/Title (India is the largest milk producer in the world, and most of that milk comes from small and marginal farmers who each keep a handful of animals. Village-level collection centres and dairy cooperatives gather milk every morning and evening, test it, and pay the farmers periodically. The price paid for a litre of milk is not fixed: it depends on the fat and SNF content found in the sample, so every single delivery has to be recorded with its quantity and quality readings.)
/Dest [12 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 2317 0 R
/Next 2331 0 R
>>
endobj
2331 0 obj
<<
/Title (Alongside milk collection, a farm or cooperative has to keep track of the animals themselves: which animal belongs to which farmer, its breed and age, whether it is currently lactating, and when it was last vaccinated or treated by a veterinarian.)
/Dest [12 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 2317 0 R
/Prev 2330 0 R
>>
