/Title (First Normal Form \(1NF\). Every attribute holds a single atomic value and there are no repeating groups. A farmer's several animals are stored as separate rows of CATTLE instead of a comma- separated list, and repeated deliveries are separate rows of MILK_COLLECTION. Every table has a primary key.)
/Dest [16 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 2433 0 R
/Prev 2452 0 R
/Next 2474 0 R
>>
endobj
2465 0 obj
<<
/Title (Third Normal Form \(3NF\). There are no transitive dependencies. Farmer details are stored only in FARMER and referred to by farmer_id elsewhere. Prices are stored only in RATE_CHART and are not copied into each collection row. Animal details live only in CATTLE. In every table, non-key attributes depend only on the key.)
/Dest [16 0 R /Fit]
/Parent 2433 0 R
/Prev 2474 0 R
/Next 2453 0 R
>>
endobj
